{"name":"Boston Fern","hex":"#90966d","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fern","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of a group of some twenty thousand species of vascular plants classified in the division Pteridophyta that lack seeds and reproduce by shedding spores to initiate an alternation of generations.","A light green color inspired by the color of ferns."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fern"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nephrolepis exaltata","blocks":[{"text":"Nephrolepis exaltata, known as the sword fern or  Boston fern, is a species of fern in the family Nephrolepidaceae. It is native to the Americas. This evergreen plant can reach as high as 40–90 centimetres (16–35 in), and in extreme cases up to 1.5 metres. It is also known as the Boston sword fern, wild Boston fern, Boston blue bell fern, tuber ladder fern, or fishbone fern."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Boston_Fern_%282873392811%29.png/330px-Boston_Fern_%282873392811%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nephrolepis_exaltata"},{"title":"Boston","blocks":[{"text":"Boston is the capital and most populous city of the U.S. state of Massachusetts. It serves as a cultural and financial center of New England, a region of the Northeastern United States. Boston has an area of 48.4 square miles (125 km2) and a population of 675,647 as of the 2020 census, making it the third-most populous city in the Northeastern United States after New York City and Philadelphia. The larger Greater Boston metropolitan statistical area had a population of 5 million in 2025, making it the largest metropolis in New England and the eleventh-largest in the United States."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/ISH_WC_Boston4.jpg/330px-ISH_WC_Boston4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boston"},{"title":"Fern","blocks":[{"text":"Ferns are a group of vascular plants that reproduce via spores and have neither seeds nor flowers. They reproduce in two phases, a short-lived gametophyte that reproduces sexually to develop a spore-bearing leaf structure. Some ferns produce coiled fiddleheads, which expand into fronds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/The_ferns_of_Great_Britain%2C_and_their_allies_the_club-mosses%2C_pepperworts%2C_and_horsetails_%28Pl._2%29_%288515393495%29.jpg/330px-The_ferns_of_Great_Britain%2C_and_their_allies_the_club-mosses%2C_pepperworts%2C_and_horsetails_%28Pl._2%29_%288515393495%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fern"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Boston_-_panoramio_%2823%29.jpg/500px-Boston_-_panoramio_%2823%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Boston_-_panoramio_%2823%29.jpg/1280px-Boston_-_panoramio_%2823%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Boston_-_panoramio_%2823%29.jpg/500px-Boston_-_panoramio_%2823%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABoston_-_panoramio_(23).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Boston_-_Old_State_House_%2848718568688%29.jpg/500px-Boston_-_Old_State_House_%2848718568688%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Boston_-_Old_State_House_%2848718568688%29.jpg/1280px-Boston_-_Old_State_House_%2848718568688%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.w